---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// Kit form 'masterclass-gate' — numeric form ID from its raw HTML embed,
// same pattern as labs.astro (labs-landing = 9705434). Tag on submit:
// masterclass_signup. Success behavior in Kit: redirect to /masterclass/watch.
const KIT_FORM_ID = '9756893';
const KIT_FORM_ACTION = `https://app.kit.com/forms/${KIT_FORM_ID}/subscriptions`;

// Copy source: podcast-studio/_showrunner/masterclass/masterclass-landing-page-v2.md.
// The current cut runs ~30 min. Change to 26 when the Nov 2026 re-edit
// (masterclass-reedit-2026-11.md) replaces the video on the watch page.
const VIDEO_MINUTES = 30;
const VIDEO_TITLE = "Why Everything You've Been Told About Getting Ahead as an Introvert Is Wrong";
---
<Base
  title="Free Masterclass for Introverted Leaders: Get Your Best Work Seen | Greg Weinger"
  description={`A free ${VIDEO_MINUTES}-minute masterclass for introverted leaders whose best work goes unseen: why it isn't a confidence problem, and the 3 moments that decide who gets ahead.`}
  minimalHeader
>
  <section class="labs-hero">
    <p class="masterclass-kicker">Free masterclass · {VIDEO_MINUTES} minutes</p>
    <h1>Your work is great. So why does it keep going unseen?</h1>
    <p class="lead">If you've been told to speak up more, be more visible, or work on your executive presence, the problem isn't you. You've been handed a playbook written for someone else. This masterclass gives you one that fits how you already work.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="container">

    <p class="masterclass-still-title">The masterclass: <em>{VIDEO_TITLE}</em></p>
    <figure class="masterclass-still">
      <img src="/masterclass-still.webp" alt="Greg Weinger teaching the masterclass" width="1200" height="676" />
      <figcaption class="masterclass-still-badge">{VIDEO_MINUTES} min</figcaption>
    </figure>

    {/* Above-the-fold capture. Only ~21% of visitors scrolled far enough to
        reach the #signup form below, so the same ask is repeated here inline.
        Distinct form ids so GA4's form_id shows which one converts. */}
    <div class="mc-inline-capture">
      <form class="mc-inline-form" id="mc-signup-top" method="post" action={KIT_FORM_ACTION}>
        <label class="visually-hidden" for="mc_email_top">Email address</label>
        <input type="email" id="mc_email_top" name="email_address" required placeholder="you@example.com" />
        <button type="submit" class="btn-primary">Watch now →</button>
      </form>
    </div>

    <section>
      <h2 class="home-section-label">Sound familiar?</h2>
      <ul class="masterclass-bullets masterclass-pains">
        <li>You had the point. By the time there was room to say it, someone else said it, and it landed as theirs.</li>
        <li>Your review says "speak up more" or "work on your executive presence," and it's not clear what that would even look like.</li>
        <li>You deliver, quarter after quarter, while louder colleagues get the stretch projects and the promotions.</li>
        <li>And somewhere in there, a quieter voice starts asking: <em>maybe they're right. Maybe I'm not leadership material.</em></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="masterclass-cost"><strong>The cost is real.</strong> Introverts earn up to $500,000 less over a career. Not because the work is worse. Because it isn't seen.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="home-section-label">After you watch, you'll</h2>
      <ul class="masterclass-bullets">
        <li><strong>Quiet the imposter voice.</strong> Being overlooked, and the knot in your stomach before a big meeting, aren't proof you don't belong. You'll see the three lies that make them feel that way, and why the quiet strengths you've been told to fix are where your best work comes from.</li>
        <li><strong>Know the 3 moments that decide whether you advance.</strong> The performance conversation, the cross-functional room, and the one-on-one, with one weekly habit for each.</li>
        <li><strong>Have your next moment picked out.</strong> You'll leave knowing which one is already on your calendar, and how to prepare for it.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="masterclass-cost">No performing. No being "on" all the time. You pick your moments and show up ready.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="signup" class="contact-form-section">
      <h2 class="home-section-label">Watch it free</h2>
      <p class="labs-next-reminder">Enter your email and the masterclass starts right away. {VIDEO_MINUTES} minutes, no slides.</p>
      <form class="contact-form" id="mc-signup-main" method="post" action={KIT_FORM_ACTION}>
        <div class="form-field">
          <label for="email_address">Email address</label>
          <input type="email" id="email_address" name="email_address" required placeholder="you@example.com" />
        </div>
        <button type="submit" class="btn-primary contact-submit">Watch the masterclass →</button>
      </form>
    </section>

    <section class="about-teaser">
      <img class="about-teaser-img" src="/greg-weinger.webp" alt="Greg Weinger" width="80" height="80" />
      <div>
        <h2 class="home-section-label">About Your Host</h2>
        <p>I'm Greg Weinger. I spent over 25 years rising to the executive level of software companies as an introvert, most of those years in denial about it. For the past two years I've interviewed the most effective introverted leaders and experts I could find on <strong>The Introverted Leader</strong> podcast. This masterclass is what I wish someone had told me earlier in my career.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <blockquote class="pull-quote">
      "I didn't become more extroverted. I became more intentional."
      <cite class="pull-quote-cite">Lissa Appiah, promoted five times in eight years</cite>
    </blockquote>

  </div>
</Base>
